Falsifies `line_editor::line_disc::verification::a_control_sequence_leaves_the_cursor_inside_the_line`.

The defect: the cursor-right move tests `cursor <= length` where it must test `cursor < length`, so
a right arrow at the end of the line steps the cursor one past the last byte. Every unit test that
presses Right does so mid-line, and none presses it at the end, which is the only place the
defect shows.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(editor.cur <= editor.len)`, on a line whose cursor sits
at its end when the sequence `CSI C` arrives.

diff --git a/crates/line_editor/src/line_disc.rs b/crates/line_editor/src/line_disc.rs
--- a/crates/line_editor/src/line_disc.rs
+++ b/crates/line_editor/src/line_disc.rs
@@ -591,3 +591,3 @@
     fn right(&mut self, out: &mut impl Sink) {
-        if self.cur < self.len {
+        if self.cur <= self.len {
             self.cur += 1;
